      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:aab5382bb626362e",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new run of words: what did lakṛī mean, and what did miṭṭī mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: भूख",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "भूख (bhūkh) — \"hunger\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "From Sanskrit बुभुक्षा (bubhukṣā), 'the wish to eat', built on भुज् (bhuj-), 'to eat, to enjoy'. The old form doubles its own first syllable, which is how Sanskrit marked wanting to do a thing rather than doing it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So भूख (bhūkh) was never the state of an empty stomach — it was the appetite, the wanting. A speaker says भूख (bhūkh) belongs to them rather than that they are it, and the wanting is the thing that is owned."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five things a body reports."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "bhūkh",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *bhūkh*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "bhūkh, then roṭī, and say which one settles the other",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *bhūkh*, then *roṭī*, and say which one settles the other]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does भूख (bhūkh) mean? (\"hunger\".) Say it once more."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
