          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "प्यास (pyās) — \"thirst\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "From Sanskrit पिपासा (pipāsā), 'the wish to drink', on पा (pā-), 'to drink' — and doubling its first syllable exactly the way बुभुक्षा does. The two words were made in the same workshop on the same day."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पा is the root under पानी, the word you have had since the water lesson: 'the drinkable one'. So प्यास (pyās) and पानी are the wanting and the thing wanted, cut from a single syllable."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two."
